  "content": "## Task\nImprove the post-route quality of `cmp32` (32-bit registered unsigned comparator: y = (a < b)) without changing its behavior.\n\n## Specification (current RTL, also the equivalence reference)\n```verilog\nmodule cmp32 (\n    input wire clk,\n    input wire rst_n,\n    input wire valid_i,\n    input wire [31:0] a_i,\n    input wire [31:0] b_i,\n    output reg valid_o,\n    output reg [0:0] y_o\n);\n\nwire lt_0 = (a_i[31:0] < b_i[31:0]);\nwire eq_0 = (a_i[31:0] == b_i[31:0]);\n\nwire cmp_0 = lt_0;\n\nalways @(posedge clk) begin\n    if (!rst_n) begin\n        valid_o <= 1'b0;\n        y_o <= 1'd0;\n    end else begin\n        valid_o <= valid_i;\n        if (valid_i)\n            y_o <= cmp_0;\n    end\nend\nendmodule\n```\nYour design must be cycle-for-cycle equivalent to this module from reset: same ports, synchronous active-low reset, `valid_o` follows `valid_i` one cycle later, and `y_o` updates only on valid cycles and holds otherwise.\n\n## Flow and objective\nYosys/ABC synthesis to the Nangate45 library, then OpenROAD placement, clock tree synthesis and routing with a 10 ns clock and a fixed floorplan. Score = 10 * WNS_ns - 0.001 * area_um2, where WNS is the worst setup slack after routing and area is total standard-cell area. Higher is better.\n\nThis RTL measured: area 268.926 um^2, WNS 7.62112 ns, score 75.942274.\nestimate_ppa on this RTL returns area 177.156 um^2, WNS 7.69083 ns, estimated score 76.731144 (estimates omit tap cells, buffering and wiring, so compare estimates with estimates).\n\n## Rules\n- One module of synthesizable Verilog-2005 (no helper modules or instances; the equivalence checker compares flat modules). The module name and ports must not change.\n- No initial blocks, system tasks, compiler directives or technology cells.\n- place_and_route budget: 4 submissions. Every submission counts, including failed ones.\n- At most 30 tool calls in total.\n\nTools available: simulate, prove_equivalence, estimate_ppa, place_and_route, finish. Your score is the best verified place_and_route score. Call finish when you are done."
